<title>POLAND: WARSAW BOURSE CLEARS TWO COMPANIES FOR TRADE.</title>
<headline>WARSAW BOURSE CLEARS TWO COMPANIES FOR TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Warsaw Bourse's board cleared wood firm Paged SA shares for trade on the main market, while clearling shares of shoe firm Ariel SA for the parallel market, the bourse said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said it also cleared new shares of automobile group Sobieslaw Zasada Centrum SA for trade on the main floor.    -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
